Here is the Siemens SCL program for controlling a Bioreactor's Dissolved Oxygen (DO) cascade and Agitator Power.

```scl
FUNCTION_BLOCK "Bioreactor_DO_Agitator"
{ S7_Optimized_Access := 'TRUE' }
VERSION : 0.1
   VAR_INPUT 
      DO_PV : Real;   // Dissolved Oxygen Process Value (%)
      DO_SP : Real;   // Dissolved Oxygen Setpoint (%)
      Agitator_Power_PV : Real; // Current Agitator Power (kW)
      Power_Max : Real; // Maximum Agitator Power Limit (kW)
      DO_PID_Reset : Bool; 
   END_VAR

   VAR_OUTPUT 
      Agitator_Speed_SP : Real; // Agitator Speed Setpoint (RPM)
      Air_Flow_SP : Real;       // Air Flow Setpoint (SLPM)
   END_VAR

   VAR 
      DO_PID : "PID_Compact";
      Agitator_Speed_PID : "PID_Compact";
      DO_Control_Out : Real; 
   END_VAR

BEGIN
    // DO Cascade Control
    // Primary loop: DO control calculating required oxygen transfer rate (OTR)
    #DO_PID(Setpoint := #DO_SP,
            Input := #DO_PV,
            Reset := #DO_PID_Reset,
            Output => #DO_Control_Out);

    // Split range control based on DO_Control_Out (0-100%)
    // 0-50% -> Agitator Speed
    // 50-100% -> Air Flow
    IF #DO_Control_Out <= 50.0 THEN
        #Agitator_Speed_SP := (#DO_Control_Out / 50.0) * 150.0; // Assuming 150 RPM max
        #Air_Flow_SP := 5.0; // Minimum air flow
    ELSE
        #Agitator_Speed_SP := 150.0; // Max speed
        #Air_Flow_SP := 5.0 + ((#DO_Control_Out - 50.0) / 50.0) * 95.0; // Assuming 100 SLPM max
    END_IF;

    // Agitator Power Override Control
    // If power exceeds limit, reduce speed SP
    IF #Agitator_Power_PV > #Power_Max THEN
        #Agitator_Speed_SP := #Agitator_Speed_SP * (#Power_Max / #Agitator_Power_PV);
    END_IF;
END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
```
This block utilizes split-range control, using the PID output to first increase agitator speed, then introduce air flow once maximum agitation is reached. It also includes an override feature to safely limit agitator power draw.

